[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The daemon is a devenv process, one per worktree

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-DEVENV-PROCESS
TITLE: The daemon is a devenv process, one per worktree
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The daemon is a devenv process, started with `devenv up` and stopped with
`devenv down`. Per-worktree isolation is inherited rather than built: devenv
derives root, state and runtime directories from the checkout path, which was
confirmed distinct across the primary checkout and both worktrees.

Auto-start on shell entry is possible but is not taken by default. A task
running before enterShell fires on every entry -- this worktree records over
seventy in a week -- so it would need the task system's status guard to probe
for a live owner first, and nothing in the repository uses that guard yet.

The process manager here resolves to `native` rather than the documented
process-compose default, with no override anywhere in the repository, so
process-compose-specific settings are not relied on.
<<<
